//*****************************************************************************
//  05_config - the STYLE dial and all tunable thresholds.
//  Edit the single RETURN line in f$Style to switch playing styles.
//*****************************************************************************

##f$Style##
// 0 = Small Ball [N]   1 = Power Poker [B]   2 = Hybrid (default)
// Runtime steering: the Terminal command "/strategy smallball|power|hybrid" sets
// openai_steer_anchor (11/12/13) and retunes the whole profile live. [steering]
WHEN openai_steer_anchor == 11 RETURN 0 FORCE
WHEN openai_steer_anchor == 12 RETURN 1 FORCE
WHEN openai_steer_anchor == 13 RETURN 2 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 2 FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Stack-depth regime (in big blinds).  Small ball requires depth; once short,
//  both authors revert to a tight raise/limp-or-push game. [N pp.33-34][B S8.3]
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$EffStack##
// Effective stack in big blinds (capped at the largest opponent we can lose to).
WHEN EffectiveMaxStacksizeOfActiveOpponents < StackSize RETURN EffectiveMaxStacksizeOfActiveOpponents FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN StackSize FORCE

##f$DeepStack##
// Above ~60bb: full small-ball / speculative play is profitable.
WHEN f$EffStack >= 60 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$ShortStack##
// Below ~25bb: stop limping speculative hands, tighten, prefer raise-or-fold.
// Also true in the Orange M-zone or worse (M<=10) for ante tables. [HoH2 p131-138]
WHEN f$Mzone <= 2 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$EffStack <= 25 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$PushFoldStack##
// Push/fold (jam, don't min-raise) at <= 13bb. Raised from 10 -> 13 per HUMAN FEEDBACK
// (learner_decisions #42: liked jamming QJs at 12.5bb instead of min-raising). [N p.34]
// Antes-aware: also jam in the Red/Dead M-zone (M<=5), which with live antes can be
// reached at a higher bb-count than 13. Additive - never removes the 13bb behavior. [HoH2 p140]
WHEN f$Mzone <= 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$EffStack <= 13 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Position helpers (relative to the field still to act / the raiser).
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$InPositionPre##
// We are last (or near-last) to act before the flop.
WHEN InButton OR InCutOff RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$InPositionPost##
// We are last (or near-last) to act after the flop.
WHEN InButton OR InCutOff RETURN true FORCE
WHEN HandIsHeadsup AND NOT InSmallBlind RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$HeadsUpPot##
// Exactly one opponent left contesting this pot.
WHEN nopponentsplaying <= 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Pre-flop sizing (RaiseTo, in big blinds).  Both authors raise BIGGER over
//  limpers (isolation) - we add 1bb per limper. [N p.24][B]
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$OpenBase##
// Standard first-in open size.
WHEN f$Style = 1 RETURN 3.5 FORCE
WHEN f$Style = 0 RETURN 2.5 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 2.5 FORCE

##f$Open_RaiseTo##
// Add one big blind for each limper we are isolating.
WHEN Others RETURN f$OpenBase + Calls FORCE

##f$Iso_RaiseTo##
// PUNISH limpers (1bb bettors): iso-raise to 5bb for a single limper, +1bb for each
// extra limper. Big enough to deny a cheap flop and play a bigger pot with the better hand.
WHEN Others RETURN 4 + Calls FORCE

##f$ThreeBet_RaiseTo##
// 3-bet sizing (to N big blinds). Larger out of position. [N pp.26-27]
WHEN f$Style = 1 RETURN 13 FORCE
WHEN f$InPositionPre RETURN 9 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 11 FORCE

##f$FourBet_RaiseTo##
// 4-bet for value vs a 3-bet.
WHEN f$Style = 1 RETURN 26 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 22 FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Post-flop bet sizing (as a percentage of the pot).  Same size for value and
//  for bluffs - never telegraph. [N p.37-38][B "reasonable bet"]
//  Wet (draw-heavy) boards get a larger bet to charge draws. [N p.231 analog]
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$BetPctFlop##
WHEN f$Style = 1 RETURN 85 FORCE
WHEN f$Style = 0 AND (FlushPossible OR StraightPossible) RETURN 66 FORCE
WHEN f$Style = 0 RETURN 55 FORCE
WHEN (FlushPossible OR StraightPossible) RETURN 75 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 60 FORCE

##f$BetPctTurn##
WHEN f$Style = 1 RETURN 90 FORCE
WHEN f$Style = 0 RETURN 60 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 70 FORCE

##f$BetPctRiver##
WHEN f$Style = 1 RETURN 90 FORCE
WHEN f$Style = 0 RETURN 55 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 66 FORCE

##f$BetPctVsStation##
// VALUE size vs a calling station. Counter-intuitively BIGGER, not smaller: a station
// pays off on its own hand strength and reads a big bet as a bluff. Bet ~pot with a
// strong made hand for max value; even overbet on "bingo" boards. [CtM p147,149]
WHEN Others RETURN 100 FORCE

##f$CbetFreq##
// How often we fire a continuation bet with air as the pre-flop raiser. [B ~90%][N ~60%]
// [T] TAO of Poker (Phillips) Ch.6 & Ch.14: in loose low-limit fields (our freerolls)
// bluffing into calling stations just donates -- "you still have to win once in a while."
// So the hybrid air c-bet is dialed DOWN (0.72 -> 0.60): bluff less, value-bet more. (The
// bot already CHECKS air vs an identified station in 50_flop -- f$Opp_IsStation Check.)
WHEN f$Style = 1 RETURN 0.90 FORCE
WHEN f$Style = 0 RETURN 0.60 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0.60 FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Draw / pot-odds thresholds.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$CheapDraw##
// The price to continue is small relative to the pot (<= ~25%): call draws.
WHEN AmountToCall * 4 <= PotSize RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$DecentPrice##
// A reasonable price to continue (<= ~33% of pot).
WHEN AmountToCall * 3 <= PotSize RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$WithinSpecRisk##
// We risk no more than ~10% of our stack on a speculative "bust 'em" call
// (suited connectors / steal equity vs a raise). [N pp.29-30][B S8.6]
// NOTE: this is a COMMITMENT-threshold (10% of stack), NOT the set-mine implied-odds
// test - for pure set-mining use f$SetMineOK below. [SSNL commitment-threshold]
WHEN AmountToCall * 10 <= f$EffStack RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//=============================================================================
//  TIER-1 BOOK EXPANSION (2026-06-15) - dials distilled from the wider NLHE
//  library and reconciled with the [N]/[B]/[T] spine. New source tags:
//    [HoH] Harrington on Hold'em I-II   [KE] Kill Everyone / [KP] Kill Phil
//    [SSNL] Small Stakes No-Limit (Miller/Mehta/Flynn)   [ToP] Theory of Poker
//    [SM] Hold'em for Advanced Players  [CtM] Crushing the Microstakes
//    [PMM] Poker Math That Matters      [MoH] Math of Hold'em
//    [SNG] SNG Blueprint / Moshman / Shaw   [EM] Ed Miller / [TN] Tri Nguyen
//  UNITS: PotSize / StackSize / AmountToCall / f$EffStack are all in BIG BLINDS
//  (OpenPPL divides each by bblind). So SPR = EffStack/PotSize directly; M is a
//  dimensionless ratio. bblind/sblind/ante are the raw chip denominators.
//=============================================================================

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  M-ratio (Magriel/Harrington) - the antes-aware depth measure. M = stack /
//  cost-of-one-orbit (SB+BB+all antes). With antes live, M is materially smaller
//  than the raw bb-depth, so push/fold should kick in earlier. [HoH2 p124-131]
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$AnteTotal##
// Total antes posted per orbit, in CHIPS (per-player ante * players dealt).
// 0 when there are no antes; degrades M gracefully to a blinds-only ratio.
// tgi_ante comes from table_game_info (set via the lobby / set_table_game_info).
WHEN Others RETURN tgi_ante * nplayersdealt FORCE

##f$M##
// Harrington M = effective stack / cost per round. f$EffStack is in bb, so
// (f$EffStack * bblind) is chips; divide by the chip cost of one orbit. Ratio.
WHEN (bblind + sblind + f$AnteTotal) <= 0 RETURN 999 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN (f$EffStack * bblind) / (bblind + sblind + f$AnteTotal) FORCE

##f$Mzone##
// 4=Green(M>20) 3=Yellow(10-20) 2=Orange(6-10) 1=Red(1-5) 0=Dead(<1). [HoH2 p128-131]
WHEN f$M > 20 RETURN 4 FORCE
WHEN f$M >= 10 RETURN 3 FORCE
WHEN f$M >= 6  RETURN 2 FORCE
WHEN f$M >= 1  RETURN 1 FORCE
WHEN Others    RETURN 0 FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  SPR (stack-to-pot ratio) & commitment. Refines the spine's "don't go broke
//  with one pair" into the HIGH-SPR case: at LOW SPR you SHOULD stack off top
//  pair / overpair. [SSNL SPR sidebar]
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$SPR##
// Effective remaining stack / current pot (both already in bb).
WHEN PotSize <= 0 RETURN 999 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN f$EffStack / PotSize FORCE

##f$Committed##
// True when SPR is low enough to get top-pair/overpair-strength hands all in.
// Opponent- and board-texture-aware. Gate the get-it-in line on this; gate the
// "never go broke with one pair" pot-control on NOT f$Committed. [SSNL SPR sidebar]
WHEN f$SPR <= 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$Opp_IsAggro AND f$SPR <= 8 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$BoardWet AND f$SPR <= 7 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$Opp_IsPassive AND f$SPR <= 3 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$SPR <= 4 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Exact pot-odds & set-mining implied-odds (replaces the coarse K-bucket
//  helpers for the cases that want precision). [PMM p59-63][MoH][SSNL p143]
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$RequiredEquity##
// Win% needed to call = call / (pot-before-our-call + call). Compare vs prwin.
WHEN (PotSize + AmountToCall) <= 0 RETURN 1 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN AmountToCall / (PotSize + AmountToCall) FORCE

##f$SetMineOK##
// Set-mine a small pair only with ~15x the call behind (real implied odds), and
// not vs a 3-bet or a tight opener (SPR too low / won't get paid). The current
// f$WithinSpecRisk (10x) was too loose for a pure set-mine. [CtM p122][SSNL p143][PMM]
WHEN f$Opp_IsNit RETURN false FORCE
WHEN AmountToCall * 15 <= f$EffStack RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Table size. The open lists are full-ring/8-max shapes; 6-max wants the EP/MP
//  seats to play wider. [V6 charts]
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$Is6Max##
WHEN nplayersdealt <= 6 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Tournament STAGE & bubble pressure. Scales the ICM get-it-in margin: tighter
//  near the bubble, looser in the money / heads-up. [SNG][KE p120-126]
//  NOTE: these depend on a REAL lobby payout curve (f$PaidPlaces). The current
//  f$icm_prizeX is a placeholder where all 8 places "pay", so f$NearBubble stays
//  false and f$BubbleTighten stays 1.0 (= today's behavior) until the real payout
//  table is scraped (lobby_fetch -> settings.lobby_info). Structurally ready.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$PaidPlaces##
// Number of paid finishing positions = count of nonzero prizes in the curve.
WHEN f$icm_prize8 > 0 RETURN 8 FORCE
WHEN f$icm_prize7 > 0 RETURN 7 FORCE
WHEN f$icm_prize6 > 0 RETURN 6 FORCE
WHEN f$icm_prize5 > 0 RETURN 5 FORCE
WHEN f$icm_prize4 > 0 RETURN 4 FORCE
WHEN f$icm_prize3 > 0 RETURN 3 FORCE
WHEN f$icm_prize2 > 0 RETURN 2 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 1 FORCE

##f$NearBubble##
// One elimination from the money. Uses tgi_players_remaining (tournament-wide
// players left, from the lobby) - 0/unknown for cash, so this stays false there.
WHEN tgi_players_remaining = f$PaidPlaces + 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$InMoney##
WHEN tgi_players_remaining <= f$PaidPlaces AND tgi_players_remaining >= 2 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$HeadsUpTourney##
// Two players left in the tournament: ICM is off, chips become linear money. [SoS p94]
WHEN tgi_players_remaining = 2 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Stage##
// 0 early  1 middle  2 bubble  3 ITM/HU
WHEN f$HeadsUpTourney OR f$InMoney RETURN 3 FORCE
WHEN f$NearBubble RETURN 2 FORCE
WHEN f$ShortStack OR nplayersdealt <= 6 RETURN 1 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0 FORCE

##f$BubbleTighten##
// Required $-equity edge over folding when getting it in. >1 = need more, near
// the bubble; <1 = gamble looser in the money. [SNG][KE p120]
WHEN f$Stage = 2 RETURN 1.06 FORCE
WHEN f$Stage = 3 RETURN 0.97 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 1.00 FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Bet-timing tells.  Hiss measures how long each chair dwells on its to-act
//  highlight (pNactive rect1) and exposes lastraiseractiontime = the seconds the
//  player we must react to took on his bet/raise. Classic Caro/Negreanu reads:
//  a SNAP (instant) bet leans weak/automatic; a long TANK then a bet leans strong.
//  Reads are noisy, so they are used only as soft modifiers, only heads-up, only
//  when a reading exists. Set f$UseTimingTells = 0 to disable entirely.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$UseTimingTells##
WHEN Others RETURN 1 FORCE

##f$SnapSeconds##
// At or below this, the bet was effectively instant.
WHEN Others RETURN 1.5 FORCE

##f$TankSeconds##
// At or above this, the player tanked before betting.
WHEN Others RETURN 6 FORCE

##f$TimingKnown##
// A sane, fresh reading exists for the player we are reacting to.
WHEN f$UseTimingTells = 0 RETURN false FORCE
WHEN lastraiseractiontime > 0 AND lastraiseractiontime < 90 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$TimingSaysWeak##
// Snap bet/raise, heads-up: lean toward it being weak/automatic. (Caro: a fast
// bet is often a weak bet.) Continue/bluff-catch a touch wider against it.
WHEN f$TimingKnown AND f$HeadsUpPot AND lastraiseractiontime <= f$SnapSeconds RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$TimingSaysStrong##
// Long tank then a bet/raise, heads-up: lean toward genuine strength. Fold the
// marginal hands we would otherwise pay off; do not bluff-raise into it.
WHEN f$TimingKnown AND f$HeadsUpPot AND lastraiseractiontime >= f$TankSeconds RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  ICM (Independent Chip Model).  The engine's CSymbolEngineICM computes our
//  TOURNAMENT-$ equity for each line (icm_fold / icm_callwin / icm_calllose)
//  from the live table stacks + the payout structure below. We use it for the
//  short-stack get-it-in decision so calls/jams are $-correct, not just chip-EV
//  (survival has value when the payouts are top-heavy). [tournament]
//
//  f$icm_prizeX = fraction of the prize pool paid for finishing Xth AT THE TABLE
//  (a final-table approximation). Sum must = 1.00. This is a standard top-heavy
//  8-max curve; replace with the real lobby payout table once scraped.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$icm_prize1##
WHEN Others RETURN 0.300 FORCE
##f$icm_prize2##
WHEN Others RETURN 0.220 FORCE
##f$icm_prize3##
WHEN Others RETURN 0.160 FORCE
##f$icm_prize4##
WHEN Others RETURN 0.120 FORCE
##f$icm_prize5##
WHEN Others RETURN 0.085 FORCE
##f$icm_prize6##
WHEN Others RETURN 0.060 FORCE
##f$icm_prize7##
WHEN Others RETURN 0.035 FORCE
##f$icm_prize8##
WHEN Others RETURN 0.020 FORCE

##f$ICM_CallEV##
// Tournament-$ EV of CALLING an all-in = P(win)*equity-if-win + P(lose)*equity-if-lose.
// (Ties are rare in an all-in and folded into the win/lose split.) icm_callwin /
// icm_calllose are the ICM equities of the resulting stacks from CSymbolEngineICM.
WHEN Others RETURN prwin * icm_callwin + (1 - prwin) * icm_calllose FORCE

##f$ICM_CallShove##
// Is getting it in $-correct? Call/jam when the ICM EV of calling beats folding,
// scaled by the bubble factor: near the bubble we need a real edge (survival has
// value); in the money / heads-up we gamble looser. f$BubbleTighten is 1.0 until a
// real payout curve is scraped, so this matches today's behavior. [SNG][KE p120]
WHEN f$HeadsUpTourney AND f$ICM_CallEV >= icm_fold RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$ICM_CallEV >= icm_fold * f$BubbleTighten RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE
